## Why This Is Asked
Explores scaling OTCA for feature flags and experiments with privacy constraints, cross-region consistency, and operational testing.

## Key Concepts
- OTCA residency and multi-tenant isolation
- Local differential privacy with per-app budgets
- Regional streaming (Kafka) and regional OLAP (ClickHouse)
- Epoch-based cross-region reconciliation and audit logs
- Testing: backpressure, drift detection, residency checks, fault injection

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP masking placeholder for feature-flag telemetry
function applyDP(value, epsilon){
  // simple Laplace noise (placeholder)
  const scale = 1/epsilon;
  return value + (Math.sign(Math.random()-0.5) * (Math.random()*scale));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model per-app budgets and monitor epsilon usage across regions?
- What failure scenarios would you validate in the cross-region reconciliation path?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical OTCA access control design with residency, privacy tagging, policy-as-code, and immutable auditing. It expects concrete choices and testing plans rather than abstract principles.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant residency and data tagging
- Policy-as-code with OPA
- Short-lived token-based authentication
- Immutable auditing sinks (S3 Object Lock/OpenSearch)
- Dynamic policy updates and backpressure testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo authorization check (conceptual)
function authorize(user, query){
  if (!user || user.tenant !== query.tenant) throw new Error('Denied');
  if (!policy.enables(user, query)) throw new Error('Denied');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy updates for zero-downtime?
- How would you model data-tags and ensure privacy classifications propagate?

