## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical design for per-tenant data governance, basic streaming, and privacy controls in a familiar ride-hailing domain. 

## Key Concepts
- OTCA telemetry path and region-aware streaming
- Per-tenant residency, retention, and redaction at ingestion
- Basic deduplication, quotas, and sampling
- Parquet on S3 with tenant/date partitions for query efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-ingest: redact PII and hash user_id
function ingest(evt){
  evt.user_id_hash = hash(evt.user_id);
  delete evt.user_id;
  writeToStream(evt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant quotas in a test? 
- How would you evolve the schema while remaining backward-compatible?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of privacy-first telemetry with per-tenant policies, plus practical exposure to a lightweight streaming path and simple data governance.

## Key Concepts

- Ingestion-time redaction and policy evaluation
- Per-tenant governance and allow/drop decisions
- Region-based streaming topology and partitioned storage
- Dashboard freshness and SLAs

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactPayload(tenantId, payload, policyMap){
  const policy = policyMap[tenantId] || {};
  const redacted = {...payload};
  if(policy.redactPII){
    if('device_id' in redacted) redacted.device_id = 'REDACTED';
    if('location' in redacted) redacted.location = 'REDACTED';
  }
  if(policy.allowedEvents && !policy.allowedEvents.includes(payload.event_type)){
    return null; // drop
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate policy drift and compliance over time?
- How would you evolve the schema for new event types without breaking dashboards?
